  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Calcium&nbsp;phosphate is&nbsp;the major component of hydroxyapatite crystal that form the inorganic portion of the teeth</p><p>Calcium phosphate&nbsp;is a mineral comprising calcium ion (Ca<sup>2</sup><sup>+</sup>) and phosphate ion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math>. It is present in the crown area of the tooth and also in bones. It contain some&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ions too. But it does not contain&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;ions.</p>"
